      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinton%2C_Dutchess_County%2C_New_York",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area that is now Clinton Corners was originally part of the 1697 Great Nine Partners land grant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinton%2C_Dutchess_County%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A 1718 road linked the Wassaic‑Poughkeepsie corridor to Rhinebeck at Crum Elbow Creek, passing through what would become Clinton Corners.",
